CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*i2s_data)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct i2s_stream_instance)...)
#488: FILE: sound/soc/amd/raven/acp3x-pcm-dma.c:274:
+	i2s_data = kzalloc(sizeof(struct i2s_stream_instance),

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

